  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "source": "## 3. Watching invariants die\n\nThe clearest way to feel the Erlangen hierarchy is to take one configuration and push it through progressively larger groups, checking after each what still holds.\n\nTake four points on a line, at parameters $x_1, x_2, x_3, x_4$, and three candidate quantities:\n\n$$\\text{distance } |x_i - x_j|, \\qquad \\text{ratio } \\frac{x_3 - x_1}{x_3 - x_2}, \\qquad \\text{cross-ratio } (x_1,x_2;x_3,x_4) = \\frac{(x_3-x_1)(x_4-x_2)}{(x_3-x_2)(x_4-x_1)}.$$\n\nNow apply, in turn:\n\n| Map | Form on the line | Survives |\n|---|---|---|\n| isometry | $x \\mapsto \\pm x + b$ | distance, ratio, cross-ratio |\n| similarity | $x \\mapsto \\lambda x + b$ | ratio, cross-ratio |\n| affine | $x \\mapsto ax + b$, $a \\ne 0$ | ratio, cross-ratio |\n| projective | $x \\mapsto \\dfrac{ax+b}{cx+d}$, $ad - bc \\ne 0$ | **cross-ratio only** |\n\nEach row is a bigger group and a shorter list. The last row is the punchline of Stage 2: even after surrendering distance, angle, parallelism *and* ratio, one number of four points survives. That the list does not become empty is what makes projective geometry a geometry rather than mere set theory.\n\nNote also that affine maps of the line are exactly the projective maps with $c = 0$ — those fixing the point at infinity. Affine geometry is projective geometry that remembers which point is at infinity, which is the one-dimensional shadow of the statement made in 1.05.",
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "source": "/* Four points on a line */\nxs : [x1, x2, x3, x4]$\n\ndist12(v)     := v[2] - v[1]$\nratio(v)      := (v[3] - v[1]) / (v[3] - v[2])$\ncrossratio(v) := ((v[3]-v[1])*(v[4]-v[2])) / ((v[3]-v[2])*(v[4]-v[1]))$\n\n/* The four kinds of map, as functions applied pointwise */\niso(v)  := map(lambda([t], t + b), v)$\nsimil(v):= map(lambda([t], λ*t + b), v)$\naff(v)  := map(lambda([t], a*t + b), v)$\nproj(v) := map(lambda([t], (a*t + b)/(c*t + d)), v)$\n\ncheck(name, f) := block([w],\n  w : f(xs),\n  print(name, \":\"),\n  print(\"    distance     \", if ratsimp(dist12(w)     - dist12(xs))     = 0\n                             then \"preserved\" else \"CHANGED\"),\n  print(\"    ratio        \", if ratsimp(ratio(w)      - ratio(xs))      = 0\n                             then \"preserved\" else \"CHANGED\"),\n  print(\"    cross-ratio  \", if ratsimp(crossratio(w) - crossratio(xs)) = 0\n                             then \"preserved\" else \"CHANGED\") )$\n\ncheck(\"isometry     x ↦ x + b\",           iso)$\ncheck(\"similarity   x ↦ λx + b\",          simil)$\ncheck(\"affine       x ↦ ax + b\",          aff)$\ncheck(\"projective   x ↦ (ax+b)/(cx+d)\",   proj)$",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": 7,
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "isometry     x ↦ x + b :\n    distance      preserved\n    ratio         preserved\n    cross-ratio   preserved\nsimilarity   x ↦ λx + b :\n    distance      CHANGED\n    ratio         preserved\n    cross-ratio   preserved\naffine       x ↦ ax + b :\n    distance      CHANGED\n    ratio         preserved\n    cross-ratio   preserved\nprojective   x ↦ (ax+b)/(cx+d) :\n    distance      CHANGED\n    ratio         CHANGED\n    cross-ratio   preserved"
     ]
    }
   ]
